Subject: Support for Alpha Processor, Inc. UP1000 systems

Hi folks...

I have just committed support for the Alpha Processor, Inc. UP1000 systems.
Info on these systems can be found at:

	http://www.alpha-processor.com/products/up1000-board.shtml

It's basically a PC-like board with whith an EV6 and the AMD 751 core
logic (same as is used on AMD Athlon systems).  SRM console software
is available for it.

These make a very economical 21246 system for anyone interested in a
Fast Alpha.

Many thanks to Alpha Processor, Inc. for providing a machine on which
to do the port, and to Bill Sommerfeld for giving the machine a place
to live and for booting my test kernels for me.

Below is the dmesg output from the installation kernel.

Enjoy!

